          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: A person reports observing two unexplained phenomena on the same night. The first phenomenon observed (12:30 local time) likely corresponds to the observation of the 60% illuminated, gibbous waning Moon, described as a \"half-circle of orange color on the horizon.\" The sky configuration at that time clearly shows the Moon in the observed sector. This case is classified A as a Moon observation. The second observation (01:23 local time) is independent, and the phenomenon's characteristics likely correspond to a kite-like object observation.",
